<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 April, from 989 to 1943.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basil-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/989">989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,037 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bardas Phokas dies at Abydos, ending his revolt against Basil II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Byzantine general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Bardas</a> Phokas the Younger died in the battle of Abydos, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellespont">Hellespont</a>, ending his second rebellion against Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a>. Phokas took part in three revolts for and against the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-dynasty">Macedonian dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1111">1111 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">915 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paschal II crowns Henry V emperor under duress</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having held the Pope captive for two months, Henry V forced him to concede the right of investiture and crown him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The concession was soon revoked, and the dispute lasted until 1122.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1455">1455 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">571 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle for Kneiphof begins in Königsberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Thirteen Years' War between the Prussian Confederation, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, fighting began for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kneiphof">Kneiphof</a>, the port district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>. It lasted until 14 July and ended in a decisive victory for the Order.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466">Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1598">1598 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">428 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry IV signs the Edict of Nantes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry IV granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">French Protestants</a> freedom of worship in specified places, civil rights and fortified towns. The edict ended the Wars of Religion until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> revoked it in 1685.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1742">1742 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">284 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Handel's Messiah has its premiere in Dublin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Handel's oratorio was first performed at the New Music Hall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fishamble-street">Fishamble Street</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, in aid of charity. It became one of the most performed choral works in the Western tradition.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1829">1829 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">197 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catholic Relief Act receives royal assent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman Catholic Relief Act allowed Catholics to sit in Parliament and hold most public offices. It was forced through by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wellington">Wellington</a> and Peel after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniel-oconnell">Daniel O'Connell</a>'s election in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-clare">County Clare</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Troops fire on a crowd at Jallianwala Bagh, Amritsar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soldiers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginald-dyer">Brigadier-General Reginald Dyer</a> fired without warning into an unarmed crowd in an enclosed garden. At least 379 were killed by official count; the massacre hardened Indian opposition to British rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany announces discovery of the Katyń graves</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> radio reported mass graves of Polish officers in the Katyń Forest near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>. They had been shot by the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> in 1940, a crime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> denied until 1990.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 April <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-ii-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis II, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1229–1294</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-iii-countess-of-flanders"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-iii-countess-of-flanders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret III, Countess of Flanders</span><span class="tp">1350–1405</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/catherine-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/catherine-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Catherine de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1519–1589</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-montalvo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-montalvo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan Montalvo</span><span class="tp">1832–1889</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-ensor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-ensor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Ensor</span><span class="tp">1860–1949</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/julius-nyerere.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Julius Nyerere</span><span class="tp">1922–1999</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-din-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fakhr-al-din-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fakhr al-Din II</span><span class="tp">c. 1572–1635</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lavr-kornilov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lavr-kornilov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lavr Kornilov</span><span class="tp">1870–1918</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-tombalbaye"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-tombalbaye.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Tombalbaye</span><span class="tp">1918–1975</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mario-vargas-llosa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mario-vargas-llosa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mario Vargas Llosa</span><span class="tp">1936–2025</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
